<h4 class="title">Securing Fair and Transparent Protection Offered by the Swiss Takeover Rules Through Being Listed on SIX</h4>
                        <p>If a company lists its equity securities on a foreign exchange, this may have far-reaching implications with respect to takeover protection. The Swiss takeover rules only apply to companies respectively equity securities that have a primary listing on a Swiss exchange. Subsequently, a Swiss incorporated company being listed on a foreign exchange may be vulnerable to unsolicited takeovers.</p>
                            <span class="teaser-link">
                                <i class="fa fa-file-pdf-o"></i>
